Note, Neural Network Studio.
Note, A general purpose MLP trainer with web interface.

Note, Error message strings.
Let msg nodata be nodata.
Let msg nomodel be nomodel.
Let msg parsefail be parsefail.
Let msg saved be saved.
Let msg loaded be loaded.
Let msg nosave be nosave.
Let regression str be regression.
Let steps str be steps.
Let loss str be loss.
Let none str be none.

Note, Global Configuration.
Let num inputs be 0.
Let num outputs be 0.
Let hidden dim be 8.
Let num steps be 1000.
Let batch sz be 4.
Let learn rate be 0 point 01.
Let halt mode be steps.
Let target loss val be 0 point 1.
Let task class be 1.
Let model ready be 0.
Let training flag be 0.
Let stop requested be 0.

Note, Dataset.
Create a list called data rows.
Create a list called data labels.
Create a list called col names.
Let num samples be 0.
Let num cols be 0.
Let data loaded be 0.
Create a list called label names.
Let num classes be 0.

Note, Model Weights.
Create a list called wh.
Create a list called bh.
Create a list called wo.
Create a list called bo.

Note, Forward Cache.
Create a list called zh cache.
Create a list called ah cache.
Create a list called zo cache.
Create a list called ao cache.

Note, Training State.
Let current step be 0.
Let epoch loss be 0.
Create a list called loss history.
Let train done be 0.

Note, Parse CSV data.
Define parse csv that takes raw text,
    Let lines be the split of raw text by newline.
    Let num lines be the length of lines.
    If the value of num lines is less than 2,
        Return 0.
    End if.
    Note, Parse header.
    Let header be item 1 of lines.
    Set col names to the split of header by comma.
    Set num cols to the length of col names.
    Note, Parse rows.
    Create a list called new rows.
    Create a list called new labels.
    Create a dictionary called label map.
    Create a list called new label names.
    Let next label id be 1.
    Let ri be 2.
    While the value of ri is less than or equal to num lines,
        Let line be item ri of lines.
        Let line len be the length of line.
        If the value of line len is greater than 0,
            Let parts be the split of line by comma.
            Let num parts be the length of parts.
            If the value of num parts is equal to num cols,
                Note, All columns except last are features.
                Create a list called feat row.
                Let fi be 1.
                Let feat cols be the value of num cols minus 1.
                While the value of fi is less than or equal to feat cols,
                    Let raw val be item fi of parts.
                    Let num val be the number of raw val.
                    Add the value of num val to feat row.
                    Add 1 to fi.
                End while.
                Add the value of feat row to new rows.
                Note, Last column is label.
                Let label val be item num cols of parts.
                If the value of task class is equal to 1,
                    Note, Map string labels to numeric ids.
                    If not the value of label map has the entry the value of label val,
                        Set the entry the value of label val in label map to the value of next label id.
                        Add the value of label val to new label names.
                        Add 1 to next label id.
                    End if.
                    Let label id be the entry the value of label val in label map.
                    Add the value of label id to new labels.
                Otherwise,
                    Let num label be the number of label val.
                    Add the value of num label to new labels.
                End if.
            End if.
        End if.
        Add 1 to ri.
    End while.
    Set data rows to the value of new rows.
    Set data labels to the value of new labels.
    Set num samples to the length of new rows.
    Set num inputs to the value of feat cols.
    If the value of task class is equal to 1,
        Set label names to the value of new label names.
        Set num classes to the length of new label names.
        Set num outputs to the value of num classes.
    Otherwise,
        Set num outputs to 1.
    End if.
    Set data loaded to 1.
    Return 1.
End define.

Note, Initialize Weights.
Define init weights,
    Note, Xavier init scale.
    Let scaleh be 1 divided by num inputs.
    Let sqrt scaleh be the exponential of the value of the logarithm of the value of scaleh times 0 point 5.
    Let scaleo be 1 divided by hidden dim.
    Let sqrt scaleo be the exponential of the value of the logarithm of the value of scaleo times 0 point 5.
    Note, Wh hidden dim x num inputs.
    Create a list called nwh.
    Let total wh be the value of hidden dim times num inputs.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to total wh,
        Let w be a random decimal between negative 1 and 1.
        Set w to the value of w times sqrt scaleh.
        Add the value of w to nwh.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set wh to the value of nwh.
    Note, Bh hidden dim.
    Create a list called nbh.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to hidden dim,
        Add 0 to nbh.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set bh to the value of nbh.
    Note, Wo num outputs x hidden dim.
    Create a list called nwo.
    Let total wo be the value of num outputs times hidden dim.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to total wo,
        Let w be a random decimal between negative 1 and 1.
        Set w to the value of w times sqrt scaleo.
        Add the value of w to nwo.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set wo to the value of nwo.
    Note, Bo num outputs.
    Create a list called nbo.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to num outputs,
        Add 0 to nbo.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set bo to the value of nbo.
    Set model ready to 1.
    Set train done to 0.
    Create a list called empty hist.
    Set loss history to the value of empty hist.
    Set current step to 0.
End define.

Note, Forward Pass.
Define do forward that takes input row,
    Note, Hidden layer zh eq Wh dot input plus bh.
    Create a list called nzh.
    Create a list called nah.
    Let hi be 1.
    While the value of hi is less than or equal to hidden dim,
        Let acc be 0.
        Let ii be 1.
        While the value of ii is less than or equal to num inputs,
            Let himo be the value of hi minus 1.
            Let wpos be the value of himo times num inputs plus ii.
            Let wv be item wpos of wh.
            Let iv be item ii of input row.
            Set acc to the value of acc plus the value of wv times iv.
            Add 1 to ii.
        End while.
        Let bias be item hi of bh.
        Set acc to the value of acc plus bias.
        Add the value of acc to nzh.
        Note, ReLU activation.
        If the value of acc is less than 0,
            Set acc to 0.
        End if.
        Add the value of acc to nah.
        Add 1 to hi.
    End while.
    Set zh cache to the value of nzh.
    Set ah cache to the value of nah.
    Note, Output layer zo eq Wo dot ah plus bo.
    Create a list called nzo.
    Let oi be 1.
    While the value of oi is less than or equal to num outputs,
        Let acc be 0.
        Let hi be 1.
        While the value of hi is less than or equal to hidden dim,
            Let oimo be the value of oi minus 1.
            Let wpos be the value of oimo times hidden dim plus hi.
            Let wv be item wpos of wo.
            Let av be item hi of nah.
            Set acc to the value of acc plus the value of wv times av.
            Add 1 to hi.
        End while.
        Let bias be item oi of bo.
        Set acc to the value of acc plus bias.
        Add the value of acc to nzo.
        Add 1 to oi.
    End while.
    Set zo cache to the value of nzo.
    Note, Apply activation.
    If the value of task class is equal to 1,
        Note, Softmax.
        Let max logit be the max of nzo.
        Create a list called nao.
        Let exp sum be 0.
        Let ki be 1.
        While the value of ki is less than or equal to num outputs,
            Let logit be item ki of nzo.
            Let shifted be the value of logit minus max logit.
            Let ex be the exponential of the value of shifted.
            Add the value of ex to nao.
            Set exp sum to the value of exp sum plus ex.
            Add 1 to ki.
        End while.
        Let ki be 1.
        While the value of ki is less than or equal to num outputs,
            Let p be item ki of nao.
            Let normed be the value of p divided by exp sum.
            Set item ki of nao to the value of normed.
            Add 1 to ki.
        End while.
        Set ao cache to the value of nao.
    Otherwise,
        Note, Linear output for regression.
        Set ao cache to the value of nzo.
    End if.
End define.

Note, Backward Pass.
Define do backward that takes input row, target, and lr,
    Note, Compute output gradient.
    Create a list called d out.
    If the value of task class is equal to 1,
        Note, Cross entropy gradient softmax minus one hot.
        Let oi be 1.
        While the value of oi is less than or equal to num outputs,
            Let p be item oi of ao cache.
            If the value of oi is equal to target,
                Let grad be the value of p minus 1.
            Otherwise,
                Let grad be the value of p.
            End if.
            Add the value of grad to d out.
            Add 1 to oi.
        End while.
    Otherwise,
        Note, MSE gradient 2 times pred minus target divided by n.
        Let pred be item 1 of ao cache.
        Let grad be the value of pred minus target times 2.
        Add the value of grad to d out.
    End if.
    Note, Update Wo and B2.
    Let oi be 1.
    While the value of oi is less than or equal to num outputs,
        Let dg be item oi of d out.
        Let hi be 1.
        While the value of hi is less than or equal to hidden dim,
            Let oimo be the value of oi minus 1.
            Let wpos be the value of oimo times hidden dim plus hi.
            Let old w be item wpos of wo.
            Let av be item hi of ah cache.
            Let step be the value of dg times av times lr.
            Let new w be the value of old w minus step.
            Set item wpos of wo to the value of new w.
            Add 1 to hi.
        End while.
        Let old b be item oi of bo.
        Let b step be the value of dg times lr.
        Let new b be the value of old b minus b step.
        Set item oi of bo to the value of new b.
        Add 1 to oi.
    End while.
    Note, Backprop to hidden layer.
    Let hi be 1.
    While the value of hi is less than or equal to hidden dim,
        Let dh be 0.
        Let oi be 1.
        While the value of oi is less than or equal to num outputs,
            Let dg be item oi of d out.
            Let oimo be the value of oi minus 1.
            Let wpos be the value of oimo times hidden dim plus hi.
            Let wv be item wpos of wo.
            Set dh to the value of dh plus the value of wv times dg.
            Add 1 to oi.
        End while.
        Note, ReLU derivative.
        Let z val be item hi of zh cache.
        If the value of z val is less than or equal to 0,
            Set dh to 0.
        End if.
        Note, Update Wh.
        Let ii be 1.
        While the value of ii is less than or equal to num inputs,
            Let himo be the value of hi minus 1.
            Let wpos be the value of himo times num inputs plus ii.
            Let old w be item wpos of wh.
            Let iv be item ii of input row.
            Let step be the value of dh times iv times lr.
            Let new w be the value of old w minus step.
            Set item wpos of wh to the value of new w.
            Add 1 to ii.
        End while.
        Note, Update Bh.
        Let old b be item hi of bh.
        Let b step be the value of dh times lr.
        Let new b be the value of old b minus b step.
        Set item hi of bh to the value of new b.
        Add 1 to hi.
    End while.
End define.

Note, Training Loop.
Define run training,
    Set training flag to 1.
    Set stop requested to 0.
    Set train done to 0.
    Create a list called new hist.
    Set loss history to the value of new hist.
    Let si be 1.
    Let done be 0.
    While the value of done is equal to 0,
        If the value of stop requested is equal to 1,
            Set done to 1.
        End if.
        If the value of si is greater than num steps,
            If the value of halt mode is equal to steps str,
                Set done to 1.
            End if.
        End if.
        If the value of done is equal to 0,
            Let total loss be 0.
            Let bi be 1.
            While the value of bi is less than or equal to batch sz,
                Note, Random sample.
                Let idx be a random number between 1 and the value of num samples.
                Let row be item idx of data rows.
                Let target be item idx of data labels.
                Call do forward with the value of row.
                Note, Compute loss.
                If the value of task class is equal to 1,
                    Let target prob be item target of ao cache.
                    If the value of target prob is less than 0 point 0000001,
                        Set target prob to 0 point 0000001.
                    End if.
                    Let loss be the logarithm of the value of target prob.
                    Set loss to the value of loss times negative 1.
                Otherwise,
                    Let pred be item 1 of ao cache.
                    Let diff be the value of pred minus target.
                    Let loss be the value of diff times diff.
                End if.
                Set total loss to the value of total loss plus loss.
                Call do backward with the value of row, the value of target, and the value of learn rate.
                Add 1 to bi.
            End while.
            Set epoch loss to the value of total loss divided by batch sz.
            Set current step to the value of si.
            Add the value of epoch loss to loss history.
            Note, Check loss target.
            If the value of halt mode is equal to loss str,
                If the value of epoch loss is less than or equal to target loss val,
                    Set done to 1.
                End if.
            End if.
            Add 1 to si.
        End if.
    End while.
    Set train done to 1.
    Set training flag to 0.
End define.

Note, Compute accuracy on full dataset.
Define compute accuracy,
    If the value of task class is not equal to 1,
        Return 0.
    End if.
    Let correct be 0.
    Let si be 1.
    While the value of si is less than or equal to num samples,
        Let row be item si of data rows.
        Let target be item si of data labels.
        Call do forward with the value of row.
        Note, Find argmax.
        Let best idx be 1.
        Let best val be item 1 of ao cache.
        Let ki be 2.
        While the value of ki is less than or equal to num outputs,
            Let p be item ki of ao cache.
            If the value of p is greater than best val,
                Set best idx to the value of ki.
                Set best val to the value of p.
            End if.
            Add 1 to ki.
        End while.
        If the value of best idx is equal to target,
            Add 1 to correct.
        End if.
        Add 1 to si.
    End while.
    Let acc be the value of correct divided by num samples.
    Return the value of acc.
End define.

Note, Save model to database.
Define save model,
    Open a database called neural network.
    Create a table called config with columns key and val.
    Create a table called weightsh with columns pos and val.
    Create a table called biasesh with columns pos and val.
    Create a table called weightso with columns pos and val.
    Create a table called biaseso with columns pos and val.
    Create a table called labels with columns idx and name.
    Create a table called columns with columns idx and name.
    Note, Clear old data.
    Delete from config where val is not equal to negative 999.
    Delete from weightsh where pos is not equal to negative 999.
    Delete from biasesh where pos is not equal to negative 999.
    Delete from weightso where pos is not equal to negative 999.
    Delete from biaseso where pos is not equal to negative 999.
    Delete from labels where idx is not equal to negative 999.
    Delete from columns where idx is not equal to negative 999.
    Note, Save config.
    Insert into config the values numinputs and the value of num inputs.
    Insert into config the values numoutputs and the value of num outputs.
    Insert into config the values hiddendim and the value of hidden dim.
    Insert into config the values isclassification and the value of task class.
    Insert into config the values steps and the value of current step.
    Insert into config the values learnrate and the value of learn rate.
    Insert into config the values finalloss and the value of epoch loss.
    Note, Save label names.
    Let li be 1.
    While the value of li is less than or equal to num classes,
        Let lname be item li of label names.
        Insert into labels the values the value of li and the value of lname.
        Add 1 to li.
    End while.
    Note, Save column names.
    Let ci be 1.
    Let feat cols be the value of num cols minus 1.
    While the value of ci is less than or equal to feat cols,
        Let cname be item ci of col names.
        Insert into columns the values the value of ci and the value of cname.
        Add 1 to ci.
    End while.
    Note, Save Wh.
    Let total wh be the value of hidden dim times num inputs.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to total wh,
        Let wv be item wi of wh.
        Insert into weightsh the values the value of wi and the value of wv.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Note, Save Bh.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to hidden dim,
        Let bv be item wi of bh.
        Insert into biasesh the values the value of wi and the value of bv.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Note, Save Wo.
    Let total wo be the value of num outputs times hidden dim.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to total wo,
        Let wv be item wi of wo.
        Insert into weightso the values the value of wi and the value of wv.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Note, Save Bo.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to num outputs,
        Let bv be item wi of bo.
        Insert into biaseso the values the value of wi and the value of bv.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Close the database.
    Return 1.
End define.

Note, Load model from database.
Define load model,
    Open a database called neural network.
    Note, Load config.
    Select from config and store in cfg rows.
    Let numinputs be numinputs.
    Let numoutputs be numoutputs.
    Let hiddendim be hiddendim.
    Let isclassification be isclassification.
    Let ci be 1.
    While the value of ci is less than or equal to the length of cfg rows,
        Let row be item ci of cfg rows.
        Let k be the entry key in row.
        Let v be the entry val in row.
        If the value of k is equal to numinputs,
            Set num inputs to the number of v.
        End if.
        If the value of k is equal to numoutputs,
            Set num outputs to the number of v.
        End if.
        If the value of k is equal to hiddendim,
            Set hidden dim to the number of v.
        End if.
        If the value of k is equal to isclassification,
            Set task class to the number of v.
        End if.
        Add 1 to ci.
    End while.
    Note, Load label names.
    Select from labels and store in label rows.
    Create a list called nl names.
    Let li be 1.
    While the value of li is less than or equal to the length of label rows,
        Let row be item li of label rows.
        Let lname be the entry name in row.
        Add the value of lname to nl names.
        Add 1 to li.
    End while.
    Set label names to the value of nl names.
    Set num classes to the length of nl names.
    Note, Load column names.
    Select from columns and store in col rows.
    Create a list called nc names.
    Let ci be 1.
    While the value of ci is less than or equal to the length of col rows,
        Let row be item ci of col rows.
        Let cname be the entry name in row.
        Add the value of cname to nc names.
        Add 1 to ci.
    End while.
    Set col names to the value of nc names.
    Set num cols to the value of num inputs plus 1.
    Note, Load Wh.
    Let total wh be the value of hidden dim times num inputs.
    Create a list called nwh.
    Let si be 1.
    While the value of si is less than or equal to total wh,
        Add 0 to nwh.
        Add 1 to si.
    End while.
    Select from weightsh and store in wh rows.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to the length of wh rows,
        Let row be item wi of wh rows.
        Let raw pos be the entry pos in row.
        Let pos be the number of raw pos.
        Let raw val be the entry val in row.
        Let val be the number of raw val.
        Set item pos of nwh to the value of val.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set wh to the value of nwh.
    Note, Load Bh.
    Create a list called nbh.
    Let si be 1.
    While the value of si is less than or equal to hidden dim,
        Add 0 to nbh.
        Add 1 to si.
    End while.
    Select from biasesh and store in bh rows.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to the length of bh rows,
        Let row be item wi of bh rows.
        Let raw pos be the entry pos in row.
        Let pos be the number of raw pos.
        Let raw val be the entry val in row.
        Let val be the number of raw val.
        Set item pos of nbh to the value of val.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set bh to the value of nbh.
    Note, Load Wo.
    Let total wo be the value of num outputs times hidden dim.
    Create a list called nwo.
    Let si be 1.
    While the value of si is less than or equal to total wo,
        Add 0 to nwo.
        Add 1 to si.
    End while.
    Select from weightso and store in wo rows.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to the length of wo rows,
        Let row be item wi of wo rows.
        Let raw pos be the entry pos in row.
        Let pos be the number of raw pos.
        Let raw val be the entry val in row.
        Let val be the number of raw val.
        Set item pos of nwo to the value of val.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set wo to the value of nwo.
    Note, Load Bo.
    Create a list called nbo.
    Let si be 1.
    While the value of si is less than or equal to num outputs,
        Add 0 to nbo.
        Add 1 to si.
    End while.
    Select from biaseso and store in bo rows.
    Let wi be 1.
    While the value of wi is less than or equal to the length of bo rows,
        Let row be item wi of bo rows.
        Let raw pos be the entry pos in row.
        Let pos be the number of raw pos.
        Let raw val be the entry val in row.
        Let val be the number of raw val.
        Set item pos of nbo to the value of val.
        Add 1 to wi.
    End while.
    Set bo to the value of nbo.
    Close the database.
    Set model ready to 1.
    Return 1.
End define.

Note, API Handlers.

Note, Upload and parse dataset.
Define handle upload that takes request,
    Let data be the body of request.
    Let csv text be the entry text in data.
    Let task type be the entry task in data.
    If the value of task type is equal to regression str,
        Set task class to 0.
    Otherwise,
        Set task class to 1.
    End if.
    Call parse csv with the value of csv text.
    If the value of data loaded is equal to 0,
        Create a dictionary called err.
        Set the entry error in err to the value of msg parsefail.
        Respond with the value of err.
        Return 0.
    End if.
    Create a dictionary called resp.
    Set the entry ok in resp to 1.
    Set the entry samples in resp to the value of num samples.
    Set the entry features in resp to the value of num inputs.
    Set the entry outputs in resp to the value of num outputs.
    Set the entry labels in resp to the value of label names.
    Set the entry columns in resp to the value of col names.
    Note, Send first few rows as preview.
    Create a list called preview.
    Let pi be 1.
    Let max preview be 5.
    If the value of num samples is less than max preview,
        Set max preview to the value of num samples.
    End if.
    While the value of pi is less than or equal to max preview,
        Let row be item pi of data rows.
        Let label be item pi of data labels.
        Create a dictionary called prev row.
        Set the entry features in prev row to the value of row.
        Set the entry label in prev row to the value of label.
        Add the value of prev row to preview.
        Add 1 to pi.
    End while.
    Set the entry preview in resp to the value of preview.
    Respond with the value of resp.
End define.

Note, Start training.
Define handle train that takes request,
    If the value of data loaded is equal to 0,
        Create a dictionary called err.
        Set the entry error in err to the value of msg nodata.
        Respond with the value of err.
        Return 0.
    End if.
    Let data be the body of request.
    Note, Read config from request.
    If the value of data has the entry hidden dim,
        Let cfg hd be the entry hidden dim in data.
        Set hidden dim to the number of cfg hd.
    End if.
    If the value of data has the entry steps,
        Let cfg steps be the entry steps in data.
        Set num steps to the number of cfg steps.
    End if.
    If the value of data has the entry batch size,
        Let cfg bs be the entry batch size in data.
        Set batch sz to the number of cfg bs.
    End if.
    If the value of data has the entry lr,
        Let cfg lr be the entry lr in data.
        Set learn rate to the number of cfg lr.
    End if.
    If the value of data has the entry halt mode,
        Let cfg halt be the entry halt mode in data.
        Set halt mode to the value of cfg halt.
    End if.
    If the value of data has the entry target loss,
        Let cfg tl be the entry target loss in data.
        Set target loss val to the number of cfg tl.
    End if.
    Note, Initialize and train.
    Call init weights.
    Call run training.
    Note, Compute accuracy.
    Let acc val be 0.
    If the value of task class is equal to 1,
        Call compute accuracy and store the result in acc val.
    End if.
    Note, Count parameters.
    Let ph be the value of hidden dim times num inputs plus hidden dim.
    Let po be the value of num outputs times hidden dim plus num outputs.
    Let total params be the value of ph plus po.
    Create a dictionary called resp.
    Set the entry ok in resp to 1.
    Set the entry steps in resp to the value of current step.
    Set the entry loss in resp to the value of epoch loss.
    Set the entry accuracy in resp to the value of acc val.
    Set the entry params in resp to the value of total params.
    Set the entry losses in resp to the value of loss history.
    Respond with the value of resp.
End define.

Note, Fine tune existing model with new data.
Define handle finetune that takes request,
    If the value of model ready is equal to 0,
        Create a dictionary called err.
        Set the entry error in err to the value of msg nomodel.
        Respond with the value of err.
        Return 0.
    End if.
    If the value of data loaded is equal to 0,
        Create a dictionary called err.
        Set the entry error in err to the value of msg nodata.
        Respond with the value of err.
        Return 0.
    End if.
    Let data be the body of request.
    Note, Read fine tune config.
    If the value of data has the entry steps,
        Let cfg steps be the entry steps in data.
        Set num steps to the number of cfg steps.
    End if.
    If the value of data has the entry lr,
        Let cfg lr be the entry lr in data.
        Set learn rate to the number of cfg lr.
    End if.
    If the value of data has the entry batch size,
        Let cfg bs be the entry batch size in data.
        Set batch sz to the number of cfg bs.
    End if.
    Note, Run training without reinitializing weights.
    Call run training.
    Let acc val be 0.
    If the value of task class is equal to 1,
        Call compute accuracy and store the result in acc val.
    End if.
    Create a dictionary called resp.
    Set the entry ok in resp to 1.
    Set the entry steps in resp to the value of current step.
    Set the entry loss in resp to the value of epoch loss.
    Set the entry accuracy in resp to the value of acc val.
    Set the entry losses in resp to the value of loss history.
    Respond with the value of resp.
End define.

Note, Get training progress.
Define handle progress that takes request,
    Create a dictionary called resp.
    Set the entry step in resp to the value of current step.
    Set the entry total in resp to the value of num steps.
    Set the entry loss in resp to the value of epoch loss.
    Set the entry done in resp to the value of train done.
    Set the entry training in resp to the value of training flag.
    Set the entry losses in resp to the value of loss history.
    Respond with the value of resp.
End define.

Note, Make prediction.
Define handle predict that takes request,
    If the value of model ready is equal to 0,
        Create a dictionary called err.
        Set the entry error in err to the value of msg nomodel.
        Respond with the value of err.
        Return 0.
    End if.
    Let data be the body of request.
    Let input vals be the entry features in data.
    Call do forward with the value of input vals.
    Create a dictionary called resp.
    Set the entry ok in resp to 1.
    If the value of task class is equal to 1,
        Note, Find argmax for predicted class.
        Let best idx be 1.
        Let best val be item 1 of ao cache.
        Let ki be 2.
        While the value of ki is less than or equal to num outputs,
            Let p be item ki of ao cache.
            If the value of p is greater than best val,
                Set best idx to the value of ki.
                Set best val to the value of p.
            End if.
            Add 1 to ki.
        End while.
        Let pred name be item best idx of label names.
        Set the entry prediction in resp to the value of pred name.
        Set the entry confidence in resp to the value of best val.
        Set the entry probabilities in resp to the value of ao cache.
        Set the entry labels in resp to the value of label names.
    Otherwise,
        Let pred val be item 1 of ao cache.
        Set the entry prediction in resp to the value of pred val.
    End if.
    Respond with the value of resp.
End define.

Note, Save model.
Define handle save that takes request,
    If the value of model ready is equal to 0,
        Create a dictionary called err.
        Set the entry error in err to the value of msg nosave.
        Respond with the value of err.
        Return 0.
    End if.
    Call save model.
    Create a dictionary called resp.
    Set the entry ok in resp to 1.
    Set the entry msg in resp to the value of msg saved.
    Respond with the value of resp.
End define.

Note, Load model.
Define handle load that takes request,
    Call load model.
    Create a dictionary called resp.
    Set the entry ok in resp to 1.
    Set the entry inputs in resp to the value of num inputs.
    Set the entry outputs in resp to the value of num outputs.
    Set the entry hidden in resp to the value of hidden dim.
    Set the entry classification in resp to the value of task class.
    Set the entry labels in resp to the value of label names.
    Set the entry columns in resp to the value of col names.
    Set the entry msg in resp to the value of msg loaded.
    Respond with the value of resp.
End define.

Note, Get model info.
Define handle info that takes request,
    Create a dictionary called resp.
    Set the entry model ready in resp to the value of model ready.
    Set the entry data loaded in resp to the value of data loaded.
    Set the entry num inputs in resp to the value of num inputs.
    Set the entry num outputs in resp to the value of num outputs.
    Set the entry hidden dim in resp to the value of hidden dim.
    Set the entry task class in resp to the value of task class.
    Set the entry num samples in resp to the value of num samples.
    Set the entry labels in resp to the value of label names.
    Set the entry columns in resp to the value of col names.
    Set the entry current step in resp to the value of current step.
    Set the entry last loss in resp to the value of epoch loss.
    Respond with the value of resp.
End define.

Note, Start Server.
Start a webserver on port 8090.
Enable CORS.
Serve static files from the folder public.
Add route GET slash api slash info to handle info.
Add route POST slash api slash upload to handle upload.
Add route POST slash api slash train to handle train.
Add route POST slash api slash finetune to handle finetune.
Add route GET slash api slash progress to handle progress.
Add route POST slash api slash predict to handle predict.
Add route POST slash api slash save to handle save.
Add route POST slash api slash load to handle load.

Say Neural Network Studio running on port 8090.
Wait for connections.
